{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["offline_access"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Plan Labor Operation"},"description":"Save a run's labor draft, as the labor planner screen does: how long the run takes (elapsedMinutes, 1\u201344640), an optional plannedStart (ISO 8601 with an offset or Z), and the complete list of who attends when (requirements, at most 50: a qualified pool by id or name, an optional named worker from it, the phase, offsetMinutes from the run's start, durationMinutes and crewSize). The list replaces the draft's requirements; an empty list plans unattended time. clear true removes the draft instead. A draft reserves nobody: commit_labor_plan does, and a committed run keeps its commitment until it is committed again or released. Name the run by operationId, or by workOrder and operationCode (list_labor_operations). Admin; operator credentials only. Preview first; the in-app assistant gets a confirm card.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"clear":{"default":false,"description":"true removes the run's draft instead of saving one.","type":"boolean"},"elapsedMinutes":{"default":null,"description":"How long the run takes, start to finish, in minutes (1\u201344640).","type":["integer","null"]},"idempotencyKey":{"default":null,"description":"Caller-generated idempotency key; required with previewReceipt to commit.","type":["string","null"]},"operationCode":{"default":null,"description":"The run's operation code, with workOrder.","type":["string","null"]},"operationId":{"default":null,"description":"The run's operation id (GUID).","type":["string","null"]},"plannedStart":{"default":null,"description":"When the run starts, ISO 8601 with an offset or Z; omit for an unscheduled draft.","type":["string","null"]},"preview":{"default":false,"description":"Step 1 of the required two-step write: set true to validate and receive a structured preview plus a single-us